<blockquote>
<p>Second is that you've gone into enough detail about the way this thing's chemistry works that I can see why it wouldn't work. That's another reason for expunging and redacting data, y'know - so that you can palm cards without having it all be seen. (There's a story I could tell you about Umberto Eco, attention to detail, and verisimilitude, but it's beyond the scope of this talk page.)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Voct, I get the larger point you're trying to make (I'm an Eco fan, for one), but your post here falls under &quot;so little detail it's useless&quot;. Which, perhaps, from a meta standpoint, you were doing deliberately, as a demonstration? Creating verisimilitude with no actual detail? :P</p>
<p>What, for you, counts as too much detail in this SCP?</p>

